      <div type="clause" n="31.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 31.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hloð ðis gedó ⁊ eft oðswerian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.21"/> wille, tio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.22"/> hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.23"/> ealle; ⁊ þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> ealle forgielden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.24"/> þone wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.13"/> gemænum hondum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.25"/> ⁊ ealle án wite, swa to ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.26"/> were belimpe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.27"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hloð ðis gedó ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.3"/> eft oþswerian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.8"/> wille, teo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.9"/> (man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.1"/>) hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.4"/> ealle; ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.3"/> þonne ealle forgilden ðone wær gemænu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.10"/></hi> hondum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.3"/> ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.3"/> ealle ón<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.11"/> wíte, swa to þam were belimpe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hloð ðis gedó ⁊ eft ætswerian wylle, teo hí ealle; ⁊ ðonne ealle forgylden ðone wer gemæne handum ⁊ ealle an wite, swa to ðam were belimbe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.14"/> hloþ (id est cohors<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.15"/> uel collectum contubernium) hoc faciat et postea negare uelint, incausentur omnes; et omnes mortis illius compositionem coniectent in commune, et omnes unam witam persoluant, sicut ad ipsam weram pertinebit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.oe.16"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="76" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif hloð ðis gedó ⁊ eft oðswerian<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Af_31-1.attnote.fn.11"/> wille, tio hie<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_31-1.attnote.fn.12"/> ealle; ⁊ þonne ealle forgielden þone wer gemænum<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_31-1.attnote.fn.13"/> hondum ⁊ ealle án wite, swa to ðam were belimpe<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Af_31-1.attnote.fn.14"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="30.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="322" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hloð ðis gedó ⁊ eft oðswerian wille, tio hie ealle; ⁊ þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> ealle forgielden þone wer gemænum hondum ⁊ ealle án wite, swa to ðam were belimpe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="65" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn eine Bande<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.de.1"/> dies verübt, [der Todtschläger<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.de.2"/>] jedoch nachher eidlich ableugnen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.de.3"/> will, so bezichtige [Kläger] sie alle; und darauf sollen alle mit gemeinsamer Hand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.de.4"/> das Wergeld [des Erschlagenen ihm] zahlen und alle [dem Richter das] Eine Strafgeld, wie es zu jenem Wergeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.de.5"/> gehört.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_31-1.lnote.de.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a band commits this, but [the slayer] afterwards wishes to deny it on oath, let [the plaintiff] accuse them all; and then let them all pay [him] the wergeld [of the slain] with joint hand and all [pay the judge the] one fine, as belongs to that wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="77" ed="#attenborough"/>If a band of marauders acts thus and afterwards wishes<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_31-1.attnote.n.1"/> to deny it, they shall all be accused, and then all collectively shall pay the wergeld and one fine—whichever is appropriate to the wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If a band of men does this and afterwards wishes to deny it<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_31-1.whinote.n.2"/> on oath, they are all to be accused; and then they are all collectively to pay the wergild, and all one fine, as is accordant to the wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="323" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If the band should do this, and afterwards wish to deny it, let them all be accused; and then let all pay the <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> communally and all a single fine, such as is appropriate to the <hi rend="italic">wer</hi>.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ofsw. <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ofsw. So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">teo <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">teo So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gylden <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gylden So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">were <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">were So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hord. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> han. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hord. So; han. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">belympe <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> to belimpe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">belympe So; to belimpe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> i <hi rend="italic">Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure after i</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ū <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ū on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> án</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to án</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ti <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ti T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">chors <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">chors R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-net <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-net Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später geänd. in</hi> tobel.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later altered to tobel.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Fränkische Rechtsausdrücke <hi rend="italic">collectum contubernium</hi> und <hi rend="italic">coniectare</hi> der Lex Salica braucht hier Q (= Hn 87, 7) und zieht dieselben Stellen in Hn 87, 10ff. aus</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q (= Hn 87, 7) uses here the Frankish legal terms <hi rend="italic">collectum contubernium</hi> and <hi rend="italic">coniectare</hi> of the Lex Salica, and excerpts the same passages in Hn 87, 10ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q, Inst. und Moderne, auch Wilda 617, verstehen die Bande (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8) als leugnendes Subjekt. Allein die Leugnung des Erfolges einer Missetat, an der so viele teilnahmen, ist unmöglich gemeint. Vielmehr macht den Unterschied gegen 29—31 hier die Verborgenheit des Totschlägers (<hi rend="italic">si non sciatur, quis nominatim fecerit</hi> Hn 87, 2; 7ff.) oder, nach Af, der Fall, dass der als solcher Beklagte leugnet. Sonst bliebe unerklärt, wieso nur im Falle des Nichtgestehens die Last des Wergelds und der Strafe vom Totschläger auf die Bande übergehe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q, Inst. and modern scholars, Wilda 617 among them, understand the band (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8) as the subject that denies. But denial of the result of a misdeed in which so many took part cannot possibly be meant. Rather, what makes the difference from 29—31 here is that the slayer is unknown (<hi rend="italic">si non sciatur, quis nominatim fecerit</hi> Hn 87, 2; 7ff.) or, according to Af, the case where the man accused as the slayer denies it. Otherwise it would remain unexplained why the burden of wergild and fine should pass from the slayer to the band only if he does not confess</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B modernises</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Händen’ Orig.; ‘gemeinschaftlich’ Schmid; ebenso Wer 4. Vorher ist Gelingen der Klage hinzuzudenken</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘hands’ orig.; ‘jointly’ Schmid; likewise Wer 4. Success of the charge must be understood as preceding this</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘nach Verhältnis des Wergelds’, technischer Ausdruck, Inst.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘in proportion to the wergild’, a technical term, Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_31-1.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vermutlich zum Schaden des Richters unter Fortfall der bzw. 30, 60, 120 Schill. Bandenbusse der einzelnen, so dass ihn eigener Vorteil zur Entdeckung des Totschlägers antrieb; gemeinschaftliche Sühne ist für die Missetäter vorteilhafter bei gemeinschaftlicher Missetat; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7. Die den Missetätern vorteilhaftere Nichtentdeckung des Totschlägers sollte nicht missbraucht werden; daher ward Reinigungseid von dem als Totschläger Bezichtigten erfordert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Presumably to the judge’s loss, the band-compensation of 30, 60 or 120 shill. respectively from the individual members falling away, so that his own advantage drove him to discover the slayer; joint atonement is more advantageous to the wrongdoers in the case of a joint misdeed; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7. The non-discovery of the slayer, more advantageous to the wrongdoers, was not to be abused; hence an oath of exculpation was required from the man accused as slayer</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_31-1.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>oðswerian</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ætswerian</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_31-1.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>hie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">teo (man)</hi>. H*.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_31-1.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>gemænum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gemæne</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_31-1.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>belimpe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">belimbe</hi>. B. Altered later to <hi rend="italic">tobelimbe</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_31-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">196</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann understands as the subject of <hi rend="italic">oðswerian wille</hi>, not the band of marauders, but a single member of it who has been accused.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_31-1.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">413</biblScope></bibl><label>it</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">i.e. each wishes to deny being the actual slayer.</seg></note>
      </div>
